### Rationale
H18 is refuted. CUTLASS cannot build 2SM tiles with batch width 208, 224 or 240. The cause is a compile-time static assert in the B-operand shared-memory layout, not the epilogue assert. The only buildable 2SM batch widths are 64, 128, 192 and 256. Measured times do not follow padded columns either, so the shipped dispatch keeps the r1 tile table. Its only change is the streaming kernel for B ≤ 16, which gives S −6.5%, M 0.0% and L +0.2% rented, 16/16 correct.

